# Fixed schema ids for wave-cycle-service (ELLIOTT-FIB-CYCLE-TOOLS). FINAL: options-edge-processing docs/ta-books/catalog/SCHEMA-ID-MAP.md (contracts 0.31.0, version 2 of WaveSet and CycleSet: 0.36.0). The five top-level records the
# service resolves at boot (BrokerGuard.schemaIds, Schemas.TOP) EVEN WITH BOTH FLAGS OFF: a registry that lacks one stops the process at start.
# DailyBarHistory is an input snapshot FILE contract, not a topic value, and has no subject.
# File column: relative to the contracts checkout's `schemas-registry/ta` directory (SCHEMAS_DIR).
# ELLIOTT-FIB-CYCLE-TOOLS revision 21 (contracts 0.36.0): WaveSet and CycleSet have TWO versions. Version 1 is the file under schemas-registry/ta/v1 (registered before revision 21 on dev and
# production as ids 2401, 2402), version 2 the file under schemas-registry/ta with a NEW fixed id (2406, 2407; free on both registries): a version of a subject cannot reuse the id of a different
# schema. The fourth column is the registry version (see es-trade-tools.map). On a registry that holds version 1 only the two version-2 rows import. The service resolves the id of its EMBEDDED
# (version 2) schema at boot and refuses to start if it is not registered, so registration comes before the new image starts. The other three records are unchanged (one version).
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.WaveSet|2401|v1/WaveSet.avsc|1
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.CycleSet|2402|v1/CycleSet.avsc|1
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.TimeframeCheckpoint|2403|TimeframeCheckpoint.avsc
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.SeriesCheckpoint|2404|SeriesCheckpoint.avsc
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.ControlCheckpoint|2405|ControlCheckpoint.avsc
# Version-2 rows after all version-1 rows so the preflight pass can see the predecessor of every row.
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.WaveSet|2406|WaveSet.avsc|2
com.optionsedge.contracts.wavecycle.CycleSet|2407|CycleSet.avsc|2
